  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({瞑想|めいそう}する = to meditate) or as a noun ({瞑想|めいそう}の{時間|じかん} = meditation time). Has gained wider use in recent years due to the popularity of mindfulness and wellness culture.\n\nWRITING:\n{瞑|めい} means \"to close the eyes\" and {想|そう} means \"thought.\" The compound literally means \"thinking with closed eyes.\"\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {瞑想|めいそう}する: to meditate\n- {瞑想|めいそう}にふける: to be deep in meditation\n- {瞑想|めいそう}アプリ: meditation app\n- マインドフルネス{瞑想|めいそう}: mindfulness meditation\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {迷走|めいそう}: going astray, straying off course (different meaning)",
